[18:15:46]   Story arc: 23 messages

============================================================
  STORY ARC — 23 CARDS
============================================================

   1. India is absorbing the largest oil supply shock in history — bigger than 1973, bigger than 1979, with no end in sight.
   2. In 20 days, both sides crossed from shipping disruption to deliberate destruction of Gulf energy infrastructure.
   3. 22 Indian ships are stranded and only 3 made it through — carrying enough LPG for three days of national consumption.
   4. Cooking gas is the real crisis: 330 million households are rationing, queues begin at 3 AM, and the government has invoked emergency powers.
   5. Even when the shooting stops, Iran's mines keep the strait closed until August — and the minesweepers are months away.
   6. —— Your refinery ——
   7. Russia flipped from a $13 discount to a $5 premium overnight, and every Gulf loading terminal your crude diet depends on is either damaged or explicitly named as Iran's next target.
   8. Your refinery's complexity score is now your P&L: Jamnagar prints money at $146, HPCL Mumbai is underwater, and the gap is permanent.
   9. The government has legally overridden your product slate — every C3 and C4 molecule goes to cooking gas first, and your petrochemical margins are not a factor.
  10. —— Your balance sheet ——
  11. You are losing ₹19.8 on every litre you sell, and frozen retail prices mean every dollar of crude increase flows directly into your loss account.
  12. The OFAC waiver covering 25–36% of your crude supply expires in 15 days with no confirmed renewal.
  13. December futures are at $69 while you pay $146 today — that basis trade closes this week or not at all.
  14. —— Your government ——
  15. Delhi refused the IEA release and is hoarding every barrel, signalling internally that this disruption will last far longer than any public statement admits.
  16. India's non-alignment diplomacy secured 3 ship transits against China's 11 — that edge is real but it is being spent faster than it is being earned.
  17. Forty percent of India's fertilizers come from the Gulf, kharif planting begins in June, and no one in the energy sector is planning for a food crisis on top of a fuel crisis.
  18. —— Your board ——
  19. At $146 crude and ₹92.64 to the dollar, your annualised import bill has tripled to $266 billion — roughly 40% of India's entire import spend.
  20. Your board is stress-testing one scenario; the three risks that could make it catastrophically worse — mine escalation, Gulf terminal destruction, and simultaneous Hormuz-plus-Red-Sea closure — are not on the agenda.
  21. —— What everyone else is missing ——
  22. Every bank model was built before March 18: South Pars is burning, Ras Laffan is damaged, and the mine clearance clock alone makes a Q2 resolution mathematically impossible.
  23. You have 15 days before your largest supply fallback disappears — lock the cargoes, hedge the curve, and brief the board before the waiver expires.
